# 04_QUALITY_ASSURANCE

## 4.1 Testing Strategy (Scoped TDD)

Not every layer deserves the same rigor. Apply the strictest discipline where mistakes ship silently,
and behavior-level tests where the user can see the result.

| Layer | Strategy |
|---|---|
| State stores, hooks, services, data queries, validators, utilities, pure logic | **Strict Red-Green-Refactor.** Write the failing test first, watch it fail, implement, refactor. |
| UI components / screens | **Behavior tests.** Write tests alongside the component focused on what the user sees and does. |
| Native builds, device flows, deployments | **Runbook + manual verification** recorded in the PR's "Manual verification" section. |

A task is NOT complete until its tests pass.

## 4.2 Forbidden Test Patterns

- Snapshot tests of full screens or pages.
- Tests that assert on internal state shapes (test behavior, not implementation).
- Mocks that duplicate the implementation under test.
- Tests that pass only because of a timing sleep; pin the clock instead.
- "Fixing" a flaky test by reordering — a mitigation is not a fix; record the root cause or the lesson.

## 4.3 Test Locations

- Co-locate next to the file under test (`Foo.ts` + `Foo.test.ts`, or an adjacent `__tests__/`).
- Cross-cutting and setup tests live in `tests/`.
- Global mocks for external services live in one setup file; per-test overrides must leave a comment saying why.

## 4.4 Definition of Done for a Workstream

- [ ] Tests exist per the §4.1 table and pass
- [ ] No regressions in existing tests
- [ ] Exit gates from the plan pass (§4.5)
- [ ] Any new gotcha recorded in `LESSONS_LEARNED.md`

## 4.5 Quality Gates

Before marking any workstream complete, run and report every gate the plan lists (defaults below;
replace with this project's commands):

- [ ] `<typecheck>` passes (e.g. `npm run typecheck`, `mypy`, `cargo check`)
